[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m [response] To determine the greatest possible perimeter of a triangle with two sides each measuring 8 units and a third side with a whole number length, we need to use the triangle inequality theorem. The triangle inequality theorem states that the sum of the lengths of any two sides of a triangle must be greater than the length of the remaining side.
