[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Substituting the known values:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ 120 \, \text{volts} = I \times 20 \, \text{ohms} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Solving for \( I \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ I = \frac{120 \, \text{volts}}{20 \, \text{ohms}} = 6 \, \text{amperes} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Therefore, the amount of current when the resistor has a resistance of 20 ohms is \(\boxed{6}\) amperes.
