[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    - The angle bisector of the vertex angle in an isosceles triangle is also the angle bisector of the base angles, which means it divides the vertex angle into two equal angles.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    - The cosine of the vertex angle is given by the formula \(\cos(2\theta) = \frac{1 - \tan^2(\theta)}{1 + \tan^2(\theta)}\).
