[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[x^2 - 13x + 22 = (x - 11)(x - 2) = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Setting each factor equal to zero gives us the roots:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[x - 11 = 0 \implies x = 11,\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[x - 2 = 0 \implies x = 2.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m So, the roots of the equation \(x^2 - 13x + 22 = 0\) are \(x = 11\) and \(x = 2\).
