[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 1. **Understanding the Function:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    The function \( f(x) = \sqrt{x^2} \) involves the square root of \( x^2 \). The square root of a number is always non-negative, so \( \sqrt{x^2} \) will always be non-negative.
