[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 2. **Simplifying the Expression:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    Since \( x^2 \) is always non-negative (it's a square of a real number), \( \sqrt{x^2} \) will always be equal to the absolute value of \( x \), denoted as \( |x| \). Therefore, \( f(x) = |x| \).
