[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 1. **Volume of the cylindrical beaker:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    The formula for the volume of a cylinder is \( V = \pi r^2 h \), where \( r \) is the radius and \( h \) is the height.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    For the beaker, \( r = 3 \) cm and \( h = 8 \) cm.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    V_{\text{beaker}} = \pi (3)^2 (8) = 72\pi \text{ cm}^3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 2. **Volume of the spherical tank:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    The formula for the volume of a sphere is \( V = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \), where \( r \) is the radius.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    For the tank, \( r = 6 \) cm.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
