[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 1. **Volume of the cylindrical beaker:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    The formula for the volume of a cylinder is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi r^2 h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    where \( r \) is the radius and \( h \) is the height. For our beaker:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    r = 3 \text{ cm}, \quad h = 8 \text{ cm}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi (3)^2 (8) = 72\pi \text{ cubic cm}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 2. **Volume of the spherical tank:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    The formula for the volume of a sphere is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    where \( r \) is the radius. For our spherical tank:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    \[
