[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[2a^2 + 4b^2 + c^2 - 4ab - 2ac = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m We can rewrite this equation by completing the square for the terms involving \(a\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[2a^2 - 4ab + 4b^2 + c^2 - 2ac = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Group the terms involving \(a\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[2a^2 - 4ab + 4b^2 = 2a^2 - 4ab + 4b^2 + c^2 - 2ac = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Notice that \(2a^2 - 4ab + 4b^2\) can be factored as \((a - 2b)^2\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[(a - 2b)^2 + c^2 - 2ac = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[(a - 2b)^2 + (c - a)^2 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Since the sum of two squares is zero, each square must be zero:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[(a - 2b)^2 = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad (c - a)^2 = 0.\]
