[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m The plant grows by 5% each day. This means that each day, the height of the plant is 105% (or 1.05 times) of its height the previous day. If we let \( h \) be the height of the plant two weeks ago, then after one day, the height would be \( 1.05h \), after two days it would be \( 1.05^2h \), and so on.
