[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m    - However, we don't need to find \( \sin(\theta) \) explicitly. We can use the fact that the triangle is isosceles and the properties of the orthocenter and incenter to conclude that the cosine of the vertex angle is \( \frac{1}{2} \).
