[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m [response] To find the speed of the particle, we need to determine the magnitude of its velocity vector. The position of the particle at time \( t \) is given by \((3 \sin \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cos \frac{t}{4})\). The velocity vector is the derivative of the position vector with respect to time \( t \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m The velocity components are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ \frac{dx}{dt} = \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right) = 3 \cdot \frac{1}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} = \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ \frac{dy}{dt} = \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) = 3 \cdot \left( -\frac{1}{4} \right) \sin \frac{t}{4} = -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4}. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m So, the velocity vector is \(\left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right)\). The speed of the particle is the magnitude of this velocity vector:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ \text{Speed} = \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)^2 + \left( -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right)^2} = \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \right)^2 \left( \cos^2 \frac{t}{4} + \sin^2 \frac{t}{4} \right)} = \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \right)^2 \cdot 1} = \frac{3}{4}. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
