[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m For 5 days a week, he spends:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ 320 \times 5 = 1600 \text{ minutes per week} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m On Saturday and Sunday, he spends \(\frac{1}{16}\) of his weekly minutes on extra learning time. So, the extra learning time on Saturday and Sunday is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ \frac{1600}{16} = 100 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m Therefore, the total time he spends learning in a week is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ 1600 + 100 = 1700 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m To convert minutes to hours, we divide by 60:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[ \frac{1700}{60} = \frac{170}{6} = 28.3333 \approx 28.33 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m So, the final answer is:
