[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m [response] Given that the units digit of \(a\) is 2 and the units digit of \(b\) is 4, we can express \(a\) as \(10m + 2\) and \(b\) as \(10n + 4\) for some integers \(m\) and \(n\). The greatest common divisor (gcd) of \(a\) and \(b\) is 6, so we can write \(a = 6x\) and \(b = 6y\) for some integers \(x\) and \(y\). Since \(a = 10m + 2\) and \(b = 10n + 4\), we can express \(a\) and \(b\) in terms of their gcd as \(a = 6x\) and \(b = 6y\), where \(x\) and \(y\) are coprime (i.e., \(\gcd(x, y) = 1\)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
