[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m [response] The position of the particle at time \( t \) is given by \((3 \sin \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cos \frac{t}{4})\). The speed of the particle is the magnitude of its velocity vector, which is the derivative of the position vector with respect to time.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m The velocity vector is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \left( \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right), \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) \right) = \left( 3 \cdot \frac{1}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cdot \left( -\frac{1}{4} \right) \sin \frac{t}{4} \right) = \left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m The speed is the magnitude of this velocity vector:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \sqrt{\left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)^2 + \left( -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right)^2} = \sqrt{\frac{9}{16} \cos^2 \frac{t}{4} + \frac{9}{16} \sin^2 \frac{t}{4}} = \sqrt{\frac{9}{16} (\cos^2 \frac{t}{4} + \sin^2 \frac{t}{4})} = \sqrt{\frac{9}{16} \cdot 1} = \frac{3}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
