[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m [response] Given the quadratic equation \(4x^2 + 7x + k\) with roots \(\frac{-7 \pm i\sqrt{15}}{8}\), we can use the properties of the roots of a quadratic equation. The sum of the roots of the quadratic equation \(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\) is given by \(-\frac{b}{a}\) and the product of the roots is given by \(\frac{c}{a}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
