[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m where:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( A \) is the amount of money accumulated after n years, including interest.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( P \) is the principal amount (the initial amount of money).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( r \) is the annual interest rate (decimal).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( n \) is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( t \) is the time the money is invested for in years.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m For Paula's investment:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( P = 10000 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( r = 0.10 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( n = 4 \) (since the interest is compounded quarterly)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m - \( t = 5 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
