[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m First, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector with respect to time \( t \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \mathbf{v}(t) = \left( \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right), \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) \right) = \left( 3 \cdot \frac{1}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cdot \left( -\frac{1}{4} \right) \sin \frac{t}{4} \right) = \left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m The speed of the particle is the magnitude of the velocity vector:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=55750)[0m \[
